{"type":"thinking","text":"Now I see the tables:\n\n- $B55E: LDA $B440,Y ; STA $0450  (min/left max speed, table at $B440)\n- $B56C: LDA $B443,Y ; STA $0456  (max/right max speed, table at $B443)\n- $B574: LDA $B447,Y ; STA $0702  (acceleration, table at $B447)\n- $B57A: LDA #$00 ; STA $0701\n\nAnd at $B585-$B588: ASL $0702 / ROL $0701 (double acceleration when turning around).\n\nSo the tables:\n- $B440: max left speed table (3 bytes)\n- $B443: max right speed table (3 bytes)\n- $B447: acceleration table\n\nY is computed above: from $B51C:\n```\n$B51C: a0 00     ldy #$00\n$B51E: 84 00     sty $00\n$B520: a5 1d     lda $1d\n$B522: f0 09     beq +9 -> $B52D\n$B524: ad 00 07  lda $0700\n$B527: c9 19     cmp #$19\n$B529: b0 33     bcs +$33 -> $B55E\n$B52B: 90 18     bcc +$18 -> $B545\n$B52D: c8        iny\n$B52E: ad 4e 07  lda $074e\n$B531: f0 12     beq +$12 -> $B545\n$B533: 88        dey\n$B534: a5 0c     lda $0c\n$B536: c5 45     cmp $45\n$B538: d0 0b     bne +$0b -> $B545\n$B53A: a5 0a     lda $0a\n$B53C: 29 40     and #$40     (B button)\n$B53E: d0 19     bne +$19 -> $B559\n$B540: ad 83 07  lda $0783\n$B543: d0 19     bne +$19\n$B545: c8        iny\n$B546: e6 00     inc $00\n...\n$B55E: lda $B440,Y\n```\n\nSo Y is 0,1,2 (or 3 for $0e==7). Tables have at least 4 entries.\n\nLet me read $B440 table. $B440 = prgRom 0x3440 = index 28 in my earlier 40-byte read! bytes[28..39] = 216 232 240 40 24 16 12 228 152 208 0 255.\n\nSo:\n- $B440 (index 28): D8 E8 F0 28 ... \n  - $B440: 0xD8 (216 = -40 as signed)\n  - $B441: 0xE8 (232 = -24)\n  - $B442: 0xF0 (240 = -16)\n  - $B443: 0x28 (40)\n- $B443 (index 31): 28 18 10 0C ...\n  - $B443: 0x28 (40)\n  - $B444: 0x18 (24 = walk max!)\n  - $B445: 0x10 (16)\n  - $B446: 0x0C (12)\n- $B447 (index 35): E4 98 D0 00 FF ...\n  - $B447: 0xE4 (228)\n  - $B448: 0x98 (152)\n  - $B449: 0xD0 (208)\n\nHmm wait, $B440 and $B443 overlap: $B440+3 = $B443. So the table at $B440 is 3 bytes (max left speeds), then $B443 is 3 bytes (max right speeds), 