{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_04_ABfmflVu6MPllT7rwbC08392","tool":"record_mapping","input":{"mapping_type":"routine","id":"0x9C22","name":"LoadAreaData - build the level layout pointer $E7/$E8 and enemy pointer $E9/$EA from the area tables at level start","source":"trace and ledgered write","length":146,"rom_origins":[{"mem":"prgRom","offset":7202,"length":146,"notes":"CPU $9C22 entry (prgRom 0x1C22) to RTS at $9CB3"}],"notes":"The routine that loads an area when a level starts: it reads the level's data pointers out of the area tables. Sequence (disassembled at $9C22): $9C22 LDA $0750 / JSR $9C09 -> area-type index into Y; $9C2C AND #$1F / STA $074F = the index of this area within its type. ENEMY DATA POINTER: $9C31 LDA $9CE0,Y (base offset table) / CLC / ADC $074F / TAY; $9C39 LDA $9CE4,Y (low byte) / STA $E9; $9C3E LDA $9D06,Y (high byte) / STA $EA. LAYOUT DATA POINTER: $9C43 LDY $074E / LDA $9D28,Y (base) / CLC / ADC $074F / TAY; $9C4E LDA $9D2C,Y (low) / STA $E7; $9C53 LDA $9D4E,Y (high) / STA $E8. It then dereferences the layout pointer: $9C5A LDA ($E7),Y reads the 2-byte area header and unpacks it into $0744/$0741 (byte 0 bits 0-2), $0710 (bits 3-5), $0715 (bits 6-7), $0727 (byte 1 bits 0-3), $0742 (bits 4-5), $0743 (bits 6-7); finally $9CA6-$9CB1 adds 2 to $E7/$E8 so they point at the first object record, then RTS at $9CB3. For World 1-1 ($074E=1 area type, $074F=5) the enemy tables resolve to $9F01 (prgRom 0x1F01) and the layout tables to $A68E header / $A690 records (prgRom 0x268E/0x2690), matching the known 1-1 level mapping. Proven by disassembly at $9C22 (no reference imported); the pointer tables it reads were independently confirmed by read traces on $9CE0-$9D6F and by ledgered one-byte writes that redirected 1-1 to another area/enemy list."}}
