{"type":"text","text":"Done. Everything is mapped, proven, and recorded; the emulator is back on the `default` hack with an empty ledger.\n\n## Constants found (all in PRG ROM, no reference used)\n\nThe jump/gravity data sits in the 7-entry \"speed-class\" tables at CPU `$B424`, selected by an index Y derived from Mario's speed magnitude `$0700` at the moment of the jump (standing = Y0, full run = Y4). The jump-init block is `$B4A0`–`$B4F9`.\n\n| Table | CPU | prgRom offset | Bytes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **JumpMForceData** (rise force) | `$B424` | `0x3424` | `20 20 1E 28 28 0D 04` |\n| **FallMForceData** (fall/gravity force) | `$B42B` | `0x342B` | `70 70 60 90 90 0A 09` |\n| **PlayerYSpdData** (initial jump speed) | `$B432` | `0x3432` | `FC FC FC FB FB FE FF` |\n| fraction seed | `$B439` | `0x3439` | `00 00 00 00 00 80 00` |\n\nThese feed `$0709`/`$070A`/`$9F`/`$0433`; the per-frame force is added by the vertical-move routine at `$BFD7`–`$C046` (the writer PC `$C004`).\n\n**Max walking speed** is `MaxRightXSpdData` at CPU `$B443` = `28 18 10` (run / **walk** / slow); the walking cap `$18` is the 2nd byte at **prgRom `0x3444`**. The horizontal routine at `$B5CC` clamps `$0057` to the value loaded into `$0456`. Adjacent: `MaxLeftXSpdData` `$B440` = `D8 E8 F0`, `FrictionData` `$B447` = `E4 98 D0`.\n\n## Routine found\n**`$9C22` — LoadAreaData** (146 bytes, RTS at `$9CB3`). It reads `$0750` → area type/index `$074F`, then builds the level's data pointers: enemy list `$E9/$EA` from tables `$9CE0/$9CE4/$9D06`, and layout `$E7/$E8` from `$9D28/$9D2C/$9D4E`; then it dereferences `($E7),Y` to unpack the 2-byte area header and advances the pointer to the first object record. For 1-1 this resolves to `$A690` layout / `$9F01` enemies.\n\n## Proofs (each a ledgered prgRom write → reset → play, then `undo_edit`)\n- **Jump force**: `0x3424` `$20`→`$04` → standing-jump apex `$00CE` went **124 → 103** (rise 52 → 73 px), `$9F` stayed at -4 longer.\n- **Fall force**: `0x342B` `$70`→`$10` → descent took ~50 frames instead of ~20, `$9F` crawled `1,2,2,3…`.\n- **Max walk speed**: `0x3444` `$18`→`$40` → `$0057`/`$0700` climbed to **63 (0x3F)**, far past the normal 24 cap.\n\nAll edits are undone (ledger empty; verified `list_hacks`).\n\n## Workflow\nCreated `eval-motion` and `use_hack`d it before any ROM write; wrote 5 `record_mapping` entries (4 notes + 1 routine, source \"trace and ledgered write\", with `rom_origins`); called `promote_mappings` once (5 discoveries promoted, 0 hypotheses skipped); then `use_hack default`."}
